+- **Semantics:** Only `PERSON` custody contributes to the person leaderboard. `OPEN` rows use current time; `COMPLETED` rows use `completedAt`. Both compare against `endsAt + checkout_policies.gracePeriodHours`. An extension made after the prior due time plus grace is a separate late episode, even when the new due time prevents a later late return. On-time rate appears after three completed or currently overdue checkouts in the window, and currently overdue checkouts count as not on time. `SHARED` travel-case/truck custody remains visible in operational checkout/overdue reports but is never attributed to the retained requester in Accountability.
